model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "A read's value that a server-rendered document carries reaches the browser as old as it was when the server sent it, on the browser's own clock: the browser adds the difference between its time on arrival and the server's time of sending to the value's time before any page code reads it. Freshness, which compares that time with the browser's clock, therefore does not depend on the two clocks agreeing. A browser whose clock is ahead of the server's reads no hydrated value again on a new document, and one whose clock is behind does not keep a value past its freshness. The 30 second freshness and every other read rule are unchanged, and the time a document spends in transit is not counted, since documents are never served from a cache. Only a success sent in the result encoding is moved; a failure is read again on first view as before."
    }
  }
}
